# Modules the guest loads explicitly at boot, one per line. Device
# drivers are also coldplugged from sysfs modaliases; this list covers
# what k3s, flannel, kube-router (NetworkPolicy) and containerd need
# before anything asks for it, plus the devices the boot path relies on.
#
# One list serves both architectures and both hypervisors. A module
# that does not exist for this architecture, or refuses to load on this
# hypervisor (hv_sock, hv_utils and hv_balloon anywhere but Hyper-V),
# is named once in boot's "modules not loaded" line and is otherwise
# harmless.
#
# vsock: exactly one guest-to-host transport can register, the first to
# load; a second fails with EBUSY. hv_sock (Hyper-V sockets) refuses to
# load outside Hyper-V, while the virtio transport loads anywhere,
# device or not, so hv_sock comes first: on Hyper-V it takes the slot
# and vmw_vsock_virtio_transport is "not loaded"; elsewhere hv_sock is
# "not loaded" and the virtio transport takes it.
vsock
hv_sock
vmw_vsock_virtio_transport
virtio_net
virtio_rng
virtio_balloon
# Hyper-V integration services (shutdown, time sync, heartbeat; the
